            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for to take off, then the Malayalam for to change."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: കലർത്തുക",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കലർത്തുക — kalarttuka — \"to mix\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കലർത്തുക (kalarttuka) is native Dravidian, the causative of the verb \"to be mixed\"; DEDR 1299 lists the root with Tamil kala, Kannada kali and Telugu kalayu. DEDR 1299 compares Sanskrit kalka."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
